  "articleBody": "Small bathrooms can feel limiting, and it's easy to fall into the trap of thinking a major remodel isn't worth it or won't make a big difference. Let's debunk some of these common myths! One widespread belief is that you can't really change the layout of a small bathroom. Fact: While extensive structural changes can be pricey, smart design choices can significantly alter the feel and function of a small space. Think about moving a door swing, opting for a wall-mounted vanity, or even converting a tub to a shower to open things up. Another myth is that dark colors make a small bathroom feel even smaller. Fact: While light colors are often recommended, a strategically placed dark accent wall or bold tile can actually add depth and character without overwhelming the space. It’s all about balance and smart design. People also often believe that you can't add storage to a small bathroom without making it cramped. Fact: Vertical storage, recessed shelving, and clever vanity designs can maximize storage without sacrificing floor space. A good contractor, like HH Remodeling LLC, can help you find ingenious solutions. Finally, many think small bathrooms don't benefit much from high-end finishes. Fact: Using quality materials, even in a compact space, elevates the entire feel and adds lasting value. A beautiful tile floor or a custom vanity can make a huge impact. Don't let your bathroom's size hold you back – let's talk about how to transform it!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-17"
